    runImaginedVideoAndReveal), but its own text now begins 1.5s after
    the video starts playing, over the still-playing video -- see
    ImaginedDaysScene.astro's own comment. The plain paper
    background-color on .experience__imagined-frame is what shows through
    only if the video never plays at all (readiness/error) or for reduced
    motion.
  */
  .experience__imagined-frame {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
    background-size: cover;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: 60% top;
  }

  .experience__imagined-canvas {
    position: relative;
    width: 390px;
    height: 844px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transform-origin: center center;
    transform: scale(var(--cover-scale, 1));
  }

  :global(html.is-fill-viewport) .experience__imagined-canvas {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(var(--cover-scale-x, 1), var(--cover-scale-y, 1));
  }

  /* Same 1% overscan as .experience__video above, and for the same reason
